From: sinful1992 <sinful1992@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 00:46:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fetch a page's trickplay manifests with one query instead of
 one per media source

The DTO loop called GetTrickplayManifest per item: item.GetMediaSources
again, then a database context and query per media source, synchronously
over async, inside the loop. ~275 ms of a 590 ms full-series episode
list on this server, for a feature that is switched off here -- the cost
is the round-trips, not the data.

TrickplayManager gains GetTrickplayManifests(items): the same media
source enumeration per item, one TrickplayInfos query for all of them,
and the same manifest shape (sources without trickplay omitted, an empty
manifest for an item with none). DtoService fetches it once per page and
hands it down; the single-item path is unchanged. Not on
ITrickplayManager, which lives in MediaBrowser.Controller.
